    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="1343" n="1303" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg1303"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">683.84A/9–953: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 659<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Syria (Moose) to the Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d659-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Damascus</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-09-09T14:00:00+02:00">September 9, 1953—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. Besides the danger of bloodshed if Israel is permitted to continue work on
                    project for diversion of remainder of Jordan waters reported in Embtel 81, September 9,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d659-f2"/> Syrian resentment can hinder or defeat any or all of
                    following projects advocated by US Government: <pb facs="1344" n="1304"
                        xml:id="pg1304"/>
                    <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>Division of Demilitarized Zone as step toward eventual Syro–Israeli
                            peaceful relationship (cf. Embassy despatch 116, August 21).<anchor
                                n="3" xml:id="d659-f3"/></item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>Jordan-Yarmuk development plan referred to in Deptel 73, September 4.<anchor n="4"
                                xml:id="d659-f4"/></item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>Any bilateral or multilateral defense arrangements implicit in
                            prospective aid programs for Syria.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Moose</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d659-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d659-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated for information to Jerusalem and Tel Aviv.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d659-f2" n="2" xml:id="d659-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 81 from Damascus, Sept. 9, reported on the Israeli diversion of the
                    Jordan River at Banat Yaacov. (683.84A/9–953)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d659-f3" n="3" xml:id="d659-f3-content">
